    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-upside potential of **Christian Yelich** and **Junior Caminero**. **Christian Yelich** leads the squad with a 72.22 efficiency score; his dynamic platoon advantage against Brady Singer is the primary driver, offering a premium opportunity to pad our HR and RBI totals. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (66.33) benefits from a favorable matchup against Peter Lambert, with his projected #3 spot in the order providing the volume necessary to capitalize on his power profile. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** faces an elite arm in Paul Skenes (64.88), his role as a leadoff hitter, combined with a 5% wind-out boost and his ability to contribute stolen bases\u2014our scarcest category\u2014makes him an essential, high-leverage start despite the SP risk.\n\nStrategic efficiency necessitates tough calls on the bench, specifically regarding **Chase Meidroth**. His 45.23 score kept him firmly in the conversation, but he was ultimately relegated to the bench because his plate appearances lack the high-ceiling platoon or SP-skill exploitation found in our starters like **Caleb Durbin** or **Josh Smith**. We are also monitoring the risk associated with **Yordan Alvarez** (44.44); while his elite xwOBA of 0.443 keeps him in the utility slot, his efficiency is suppressed today by a challenging same-handed matchup against Ian Seymour and a park factor penalty. Meanwhile, **Carson Benge** represents our most precarious start, as his 51.46 score is heavily reliant on lineup position against Gerrit Cole; should he drop in the order, his value may vanish. We remain without the services of **Casey Schmitt** and **Dillon Dingler** due to injury and lineup unavailability, respectively, leaving **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** and **Jacob Gonzalez** in reserve as we monitor late-breaking lineup changes for **Gary Sanchez**, **Trea Turner**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Yordan Alvarez**.",
